      "worked_solution": "To plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y = \\tan x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $3$ units **down.**\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y = \\tan x - 3.$ \n\nSo, we conclude that $D = -3.$",
